# 4-Hydroxybenzoic acid (para-hydroxybenzoic acid, p-HBA)
# pKa1=4.540 (COOH, q=0→-1)
# pKa2=9.460 (phenol OH, q=-1→-2)
# Source: Perrin 1981 / NIST
# The para-OH raises carboxylate pKa slightly (+M donation) while the
# carboxylate EW group lowers the phenol pKa (9.46 vs 9.99).
# Important: tests whether GPR correctly handles mutual FG influence
# across a benzene ring in a polyprotic compound.

